From dd2babac2bfe8cd086c2e8571a72f33da13c644b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:12:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/32] B70-QSA-D03: C2 scorer launch defaults on XPU (bf16
 indexer)

From the Triton scorer sweep (candidate tune.json, Triton 3.8.0+xpu, B70):
decode_score: num_warps 4, stages 3, block_n 32, tiles_per_prog 1. This is the lowest
max-regret row, worst 1.15x of the per-shape best over 8/64 rows x 4K/131K; the old
default was 1.5-3.5x slower.
prefill_score: tile_r 32, block_n 128, k_tiles 16, stages 1, num_warps 16, the 131K winner
(11x). The sweep qualified it on 7 sampled rows, and its warps-2 sibling selects wrong, so
the full-row check (B70_BENCH_CHECK_ROWS=all) gates it on the next GPU window.

fp8 indexer unchanged (never swept). B70_QSA_TUNE still overrides every field;
B70_QSA_SCORE_DEFAULTS=legacy restores the GB300 copies. dtype is threaded into
_decode_block_n / _decode_tiles_per_program (None = bf16, the bench's dtype).
